  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nRidging will build back in over the Great Basin come Sunday, \nleading to near normal temperatures and generally dry conditions\nthrough Monday. Barring a slight chance (10-20%) of afternoon \nshowers and thunderstorms over the Central ID Mountains. Come \nTuesday, a quick short-wave looks to approach from the \nnorthwest, reintroducing breezy conditions and precipitation \nchances. Moisture looks to be more limited this time around, \nwith the best chances of precipitation (15-35%) over higher \nterrain. Beyond Wednesday, guidance hints at a ridge building \nback in over the great basin, support another warming and drying\ntrend.",
